Default value: false.

If both the launch template and the launch configurations are specified, the launch template takes precedence.', example='false'),
      KMSKeyId?: string(name='KMSKeyId', description='The KMS key ID of the system disk.

When both a launch template and launch configuration information are specified, the launch template takes precedence.', example='0e478b7a-4262-4802-b8cb-00d3fb40****'),
      provisionedIops?: long(name='ProvisionedIops', description='The provisioned read/write IOPS of the ESSD AutoPL disk. Valid values: 0 to min{50,000, 1000 × Capacity - Baseline performance}.

Baseline performance = min{1,800 + 50 × Capacity, 50,000}.
> This parameter is supported only when the SystemDisk.Category parameter is set to cloud_auto. For more information, see [ESSD AutoPL disks](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/368372.html).', example='40000'),
    }(name='SystemDisk', description='The system disk configuration of the instance. If both the launch template and the launch configurations are specified, the launch template takes precedence.'),
    systemDiskCategory?: string(name='SystemDiskCategory', description='The category of the system disk. Valid values:

- cloud_efficiency: ultra disk.
- cloud_ssd: standard SSD.
- cloud_essd: enterprise SSD.
- cloud: basic disk.

The default value is cloud for retired instance types that are not I/O optimization instances, and cloud_efficiency for other instance types.

If you specify both a launch template and launch configurations, the system preferentially uses the launch template.', example='cloud_ssd'),
    systemDiskDescription?: string(name='SystemDiskDescription', description='The description of the system disk. The description must be 2 to 256 characters in length and cannot start with `http://` or `https://`.

If you specify both a launch template and launch configurations, the system preferentially uses the launch template.', example='SystemDisk_Description'),
    systemDiskName?: string(name='SystemDiskName', description='The name of the system disk. The name must be 2 to 128 characters in length. It must start with a letter or a Chinese character and cannot start with `http://` or `https://`. It can contain digits, periods (.), colons (:), underscores (_), and hyphens (-).

Default value: null.

If you specify both a launch template and launch configurations, the system preferentially uses the launch template.', example='cloud_ssdSystem'),
    systemDiskPerformanceLevel?: string(name='SystemDiskPerformanceLevel', description='The performance level Settings for the standard SSD used as the system disk. Valid values:

- PL0 (default): A single enterprise SSD can deliver up to 10,000 random read/write IOPS.
- PL1: A single enterprise SSD can deliver up to 50,000 random read/write IOPS.
- PL2: A single enterprise SSD can deliver up to 100,000 random read/write IOPS.
- PL3: A single enterprise SSD can deliver up to 1,000,000 random read/write IOPS.

For more information about how to select an enterprise SSD performance level, see [enterprise SSDs](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/122389.html).

If you specify both a launch template and launch configurations, the system preferentially uses the launch template.', example='PL0'),
    systemDiskSize?: int32(name='SystemDiskSize', description='The size of the system disk. Unit: GiB. Valid values: 20 to 500. The value of this parameter must be greater than or equal to max{20, the size of the image specified by LaunchConfiguration.ImageId}.

Default value: max{40, the size of the image specified by LaunchConfiguration.ImageId}.

If you specify both a launch template and launch configurations, the system preferentially uses the launch template.', example='40'),
    tag?: [ 
      {
        key?: string(name='Key', description='The tag key of the instance. Valid values of N: 1 to 20. If this parameter is specified, it cannot be an empty string. The tag key can be up to 128 characters in length. It cannot start with aliyun or acs:, and cannot contain http:// or https://. If both the launch template and the launch configurations are specified, the launch template takes precedence.', example='TestKey'),
        value?: string(name='Value', description='The tag value of the instance. Valid values of N: 1 to 20. If this parameter is specified, it can be an empty string. The tag value can be up to 128 characters in length. It cannot start with acs:, and cannot contain http:// or https://. If both the launch template and the launch configurations are specified, the launch template takes precedence.', example='TestValue'),
      }
    ](name='Tag', description='The extended list of tags for the launch template.'),
    userData?: string(name='UserData', description='Instance user data of the instance. Instance user data must be encoded in Base64. The maximum size of the raw data is 32 KB. If you specify both a launch template and launch configurations, the system preferentially uses the launch template.', example='ZWNobyBoZWxsbyBlY3Mh'),
    autoRenew?: boolean(name='AutoRenew', description='Specifies whether to enable auto-renewal. This parameter takes effect when you create subscription instances. Valid values:

- true: Auto-renewal is enabled.
- false (default): Auto-renewal is disabled.', example='true'),
    autoRenewPeriod?: int32(name='AutoRenewPeriod', description='The auto-renewal period. Valid values: 
         
<props="china">
- When PeriodUnit is set to Week: 1, 2, and 3.
- When PeriodUnit is set to Month: 1, 2, 3, 6, 12, 24, 36, 48, and 60.



