      description?: string(name='Description', description='The description of the Elastic Network Interface (ENI).

Take note of the following items:

- The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.
- The description must be 2 to 256 characters in length and cannot start with `http://` or `https://`.
- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`, you do not need to specify this parameter.', example='Network_Description'),
      instanceType?: string(name='InstanceType', description='The type of the Elastic Network Interface (ENI). The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.

Valid values:

- Primary: primary ENI.
- Secondary: secondary ENI.

Default value: Secondary.', example='Secondary'),
      ipv6Address?: [ string ](name='Ipv6Address', description='Specifies one or more IPv6 addresses for the primary ENI. You can specify up to 10 IPv6 addresses. Valid values of the second N: 1 to 10.

Example: `Ipv6Address.1=2001:db8:1234:1a00::***`

Note:

- This parameter takes effect only when `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`. If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Secondary` or left empty, you cannot specify this parameter.

- After you specify this parameter, the value of `Amount` can only be 1, and you cannot specify `Ipv6AddressCount`, `Ipv6Address.N`, or `NetworkInterface.N.Ipv6AddressCount`.'),
      ipv6AddressCount?: long(name='Ipv6AddressCount', description='Specifies the number of randomly generated IPv6 addresses for the primary ENI. Valid values: 1 to 10.

Note:

- This parameter takes effect only when `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`. If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Secondary` or left empty, you cannot specify this parameter.

- After you specify this parameter, you cannot specify `Ipv6AddressCount`, `Ipv6Address.N`, or `NetworkInterface.N.Ipv6Address.N`.', example='1'),
      networkCardIndex?: int32(name='NetworkCardIndex', description='The index of the physical network card to which the network interface controller (NIC) is bound.

Take note of the following items:
- Only specific instance types support specifying the physical network card index.
- When NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType is set to Primary, if the instance type supports physical network cards and you specify this parameter, it can only be set to 0.
- When NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType is set to Secondary or left empty, if the instance type supports physical network cards, this parameter can be configured based on the instance type. For more information, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html).', example='0'),
      networkInterfaceId?: string(name='NetworkInterfaceId', description='The ID of the Elastic Network Interface (ENI) to be attached to the instance.

After this parameter is specified, `Amount` can only be set to 1.

> This parameter takes effect only for secondary ENIs. After you specify an existing secondary ENI, you cannot configure other ENI creation parameters.', example='eni-bp1gn106np8jhxhj****'),
      networkInterfaceName?: string(name='NetworkInterfaceName', description='The name of the Elastic Network Interface (ENI). The name must be 2 to 128 characters in length and can contain letters and digits in the Unicode Letter categorization. It can also contain colons (:), underscores (_), periods (.), and hyphens (-).

Take note of the following items:

- The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`, you do not need to specify this parameter.', example='Network_Name'),
      networkInterfaceTrafficMode?: string(name='NetworkInterfaceTrafficMode', description='The communication mode of the network interface controller (NIC). Valid values:

- Standard: uses the TCP communication mode.
- HighPerformance: enables the Elastic RDMA Interface (ERI) and uses the RDMA communication mode.

Default value: Standard.

> The number of Elastic Network Interfaces (ENIs) in RDMA mode cannot exceed the limit of the instance family. For more information, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html).', example='Standard'),
      primaryIpAddress?: string(name='PrimaryIpAddress', description='Adds an Elastic Network Interface (ENI) and specifies its primary IP address.

Take note of the following items:

- The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.
    - When you configure one network interface controller (NIC), you can configure one primary network interface controller (NIC) or one secondary ENI. If the `Amount` parameter is set to a value greater than 1, and a primary network interface controller (NIC) is configured along with this parameter, it indicates that when multiple ECS instances are created in a batch, consecutive primary IP addresses are allocated to the ECS instances starting from the specified primary IP address. Note that in this case, you cannot attach secondary ENIs to target instances.
    - Note that if the `Amount` parameter is set to a value greater than 1 and this parameter is configured for the primary network interface controller (NIC), you cannot configure secondary ENIs (that is, you cannot set `NetworkInterface.2.InstanceType=Secondary`).

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`, this parameter functions the same as `PrivateIpAddress`. Note that you cannot configure both this parameter and the `PrivateIpAddress` parameter at the same time.

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Secondary` or left empty, this parameter specifies the primary IP address for the secondary ENI. By default, an IP address is randomly selected from the vSwitch CIDR block of the vSwitch to which the network interface controller (NIC) belongs.

>- The first and the last three IP addresses of each vSwitch are system reserved IP addresses and cannot be specified.
For example, if the vSwitch CIDR block is 192.168.1.0/24, the IP addresses 192.168.1.0, 192.168.1.253, 192.168.1.254, and 192.168.1.255 are system reserved IP addresses.', example='``172.16.**.**``'),
      queueNumber?: int32(name='QueueNumber', description='The number of queues for the Elastic Network Interface (ENI).

Take note of the following items:

- The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.

- The value cannot exceed the maximum number of queues per network interface controller (NIC) allowed by the target instance type.

- The total number of queues for all network interface controllers (NICs) of the target instance cannot exceed the total queue quota allowed by the target instance type. You can query the `MaximumQueueNumberPerEni` and `TotalEniQueueQuantity` fields by calling the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25620.html) operation to obtain the maximum number of queues per network interface controller (NIC) and the total queue quota for the target instance type.

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary` and this parameter is specified, you cannot specify the `NetworkInterfaceQueueNumber` parameter.', example='8'),
      queuePairNumber?: long(name='QueuePairNumber', description='The number of queue pairs for the RDMA ENI.

If you want to attach multiple RDMA ENIs to the instance, we recommend that you manually specify the `QueuePairNumber` for each ENI based on the maximum `QueuePairNumber` supported by the instance type and the number of ENIs you plan to use. Make sure that the total number of queue pairs for all ENIs does not exceed the maximum value allowed by the instance type. You can call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the maximum value for the instance type.

>Notice: If `QueuePairNumber` is not specified for an RDMA ENI, the maximum `QueuePairNumber` supported by the instance type for all RDMA ENIs is used by default. Therefore, after you attach an RDMA ENI for which `QueuePairNumber` is not specified, you cannot attach more RDMA ENIs (regular ENIs are not subject to this limit).</notice>', example='0'),
      rxQueueSize?: int32(name='RxQueueSize', description='The inbound queue depth of the Elastic Network Interface (ENI).


<props="china">

>This parameter is in invitational preview and is not yet available. If you need to use it, [submit a ticket](https://selfservice.console.aliyun.com/ticket/createIndex) to apply for whitelist access.






<props="intl">

> This parameter is in invitational preview and is not yet available. If you need to use it, [submit a ticket](https://smartservice.console.aliyun.com/service/create-ticket-intl) to apply for whitelist access.



When you use this parameter, take note of the following items:

- It applies only to ECS instance types of Generation 7 and later.

- It currently applies only to Linux images.

- A larger inbound queue depth can improve inbound throughput and reduce the packet loss rate, but it consumes more memory.', example='8192'),
      secondaryPrivateIpAddressCount?: int32(name='SecondaryPrivateIpAddressCount', description='The number of secondary private IPv4 addresses to allocate to the network interface controller (NIC). Valid values: 1 to 49.

- The value cannot exceed the limit on the number of IP addresses for the instance type. For more information, see [Instance families](~~~25378~~).
- `NetworkInterface.N.SecondaryPrivateIpAddressCount` specifies the number of secondary private IPv4 addresses to allocate to the network interface controller (NIC) (excluding the primary private IP address of the network interface controller (NIC)). The system randomly allocates these addresses from the active CIDR block of the vSwitch (`NetworkInterface.N.VSwitchId`) to which the network interface controller (NIC) belongs.', example='10'),
      securityGroupId?: string(name='SecurityGroupId', description='The ID of the security group to which the Elastic Network Interface (ENI) belongs.

Take note of the following items:

- The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`, you must specify this parameter. In this case, this parameter functions the same as `SecurityGroupId`. Note that you cannot specify `SecurityGroupId`, `SecurityGroupIds.N`, or `NetworkInterface.N.SecurityGroupIds.N` at the same time.

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Secondary` or left empty, this parameter is optional. The default value is the security group to which the ECS instance belongs.', example='sg-bp67acfmxazb4p****'),
      securityGroupIds?: [ string ](name='SecurityGroupIds', description='The IDs of one or more security groups to which the Elastic Network Interface (ENI) belongs.

- The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.
- The second N indicates that you can specify one or more security group IDs. The valid values of N depend on the quota of security groups that the instance can join. For more information, see [Security group limits](~~25412#SecurityGroupQuota1~~).

Take note of the following items:

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`, you must specify this parameter or `NetworkInterface.N.SecurityGroupId`. In this case, this parameter functions the same as `SecurityGroupIds.N`. Note that you cannot specify `SecurityGroupId`, `SecurityGroupIds.N`, or `NetworkInterface.N.SecurityGroupId` at the same time.

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Secondary` or left empty, this parameter is optional. The default value is the security group to which the ECS instance belongs.', example='sg-bp15ed6xe1yxeycg7****'),
      sourceDestCheck?: boolean(name='SourceDestCheck', description='Specifies whether to enable the source/destination checking feature. We recommend that you enable this feature to improve network security. Valid values:

- true: Yes.

- false: No.

Default value: false.

> This feature is supported only in specific regions. Before you use this feature, read [Source/destination checking](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2863210.html) carefully.', example='false'),
      txQueueSize?: int32(name='TxQueueSize', description='The outbound queue depth of the Elastic Network Interface (ENI).


<props="china">

>This parameter is in invitational preview and is not yet available. If you need to use it, [submit a ticket](https://selfservice.console.aliyun.com/ticket/createIndex) to apply for whitelist access.






<props="intl">

> This parameter is in invitational preview and is not yet available. If you need to use it, [submit a ticket](https://smartservice.console.aliyun.com/service/create-ticket-intl) to apply for whitelist access.



When you use this parameter, take note of the following items:

- It applies only to ECS instance types of Generation 7 and later.

- It currently applies only to Linux images.

- A larger outbound queue depth can improve outbound throughput and reduce the packet loss rate, but it consumes more memory.', example='8192'),
      vSwitchId?: string(name='VSwitchId', description='The ID of the vSwitch to which the Elastic Network Interface (ENI) belongs.

Take note of the following items:

- The value of N cannot exceed the maximum number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the instance type. For more information about the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by an instance type, see [Instance families](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25378.html) or call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2679699.html) operation to query the number of network interface controllers (NICs) supported by the target instance type.  
- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Primary`, you must specify this parameter. In this case, this parameter functions the same as `VSwitchId`. Note that you cannot specify both this parameter and the `VSwitchId` parameter at the same time.

- If `NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType` is set to `Secondary` or left empty, this parameter is optional. The default value is the vSwitch to which the ECS instance belongs.', example='vsw-bp67acfmxazb4p****'),
    }
  ](name='NetworkInterface', description='The elastic network interface (ENI) information.', position='Query'),
  networkInterfaceQueueNumber?: int32(name='NetworkInterfaceQueueNumber', description='The number of queues for the primary ENI. Take note of the following items:

- The value cannot exceed the maximum number of queues per ENI allowed by the instance type.

- The total number of queues for all ENIs of the instance cannot exceed the total queue quota allowed by the instance type. You can call the [DescribeInstanceTypes](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25620.html) operation to query the MaximumQueueNumberPerEni and TotalEniQueueQuantity fields for the maximum number of queues per ENI and the total quota of the instance type.

- If NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType is set to Primary, you cannot set NetworkInterfaceQueueNumber. You can only set NetworkInterface.N.QueueNumber.', example='8', minimum=1, position='Query'),
  networkOptions?: {
    bandwidthWeighting?: string(name='BandwidthWeighting', description='The bandwidth weight of the instance. The valid values vary based on the instance type. You can call the DescribeInstanceTypes operation to query the valid values for a specific instance type. The BandwidthWeighting field in the response indicates the bandwidth weight levels supported by the instance type. You can use the name field in the response as the dictionary value, such as Vpc-L1 or Ebs-L1.', example='Default'),
    enableJumboFrame?: boolean(name='EnableJumboFrame', description='Specifies whether to enable the jumbo frame feature for the instance. Valid values:

- false: The jumbo frame feature is disabled. The maximum transmission unit (MTU) of all ENIs (including the primary ENI and secondary ENIs) under the instance is set to 1500.

- true: The jumbo frame feature is enabled. The MTU of all ENIs (including the primary ENI and secondary ENIs) under the instance is set to 8500.

Default value: true.

> The jumbo frame feature is supported only by specific eighth-generation and later instance types. For more information, see [MTU of ECS instances](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/200512.html).', example='false'),
    enableNetworkEncryption?: boolean(name='EnableNetworkEncryption', description='> This parameter is in invitational preview and is not available.'),
  }(name='NetworkOptions', description='The network attribute parameters.', position='Query'),
  ownerAccount?: string(name='OwnerAccount', position='Query'),
  ownerId?: long(name='OwnerId', position='Query'),
  password?: string(name='Password', description='The instance password. The password must be 8 to 30 characters in length and must contain at least three of the following character types: uppercase letters, lowercase letters, digits, and special characters. The special characters can be:

```
()`~!@#$%^&*-_+=|{}[]:;\\\\"<>,.?/
```

For Windows instances, the password cannot start with a forward slash (/).

> If you specify the Password parameter, send the request over HTTPS to prevent password leaks.', example='EcsV587!', position='Query'),
  passwordInherit?: boolean(name='PasswordInherit', description='Specifies whether to use the preset password of the image. Valid values:

- true: Uses the preset password.
- false: Does not use the preset password.

Default value: false.

> If you specify this parameter, the Password parameter must be left empty. Make sure that the image you use has a preset password.', example='false', position='Query'),
  period?: int32(name='Period', description='The subscription duration of the resource. The unit is specified by PeriodUnit. This parameter takes effect and is required only when the InstanceChargeType parameter is set to PrePaid. If DedicatedHostId is specified, the subscription duration cannot exceed the subscription duration of the dedicated host. Valid values:

<props="china">
- When PeriodUnit is set to Week, valid values of Period are 1, 2, 3, and 4.
- When PeriodUnit is set to Month, valid values of Period are 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 12, 24, 36, 48, and 60.



<props="intl">When PeriodUnit is set to Month, valid values of Period are 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 12, 24, 36, 48, and 60.', example='1', position='Query'),
  periodUnit?: string(name='PeriodUnit', description='The time unit for the subscription billing method. Valid values: 

<props="china">
- Week.
- Month (default).



<props="intl">Month (default).', example='Month', position='Query'),
  privateDnsNameOptions?: {
    enableInstanceIdDnsAAAARecord?: boolean(name='EnableInstanceIdDnsAAAARecord', description='Specifies whether to enable or disable the resolution of instance ID-based domain names to IPv6 addresses. Valid values:

- true: Enabled.

- false: Disabled.

Default value: false.', example='true'),
    enableInstanceIdDnsARecord?: boolean(name='EnableInstanceIdDnsARecord', description='Specifies whether to enable or disable the resolution of instance ID-based domain names to IPv4 addresses. Valid values:

- true: Enabled.

- false: Disabled.

Default value: false.', example='false'),
    enableIpDnsARecord?: boolean(name='EnableIpDnsARecord', description='Specifies whether to enable or disable the resolution of IP-based domain names to IPv4 addresses. Valid values:

- true: Enabled.
- false: Disabled.

Default value: false.', example='true'),
    enableIpDnsPtrRecord?: boolean(name='EnableIpDnsPtrRecord', description='Specifies whether to enable or disable the reverse resolution of IPv4 addresses to IP-based domain names. Valid values:

- true: Enabled.
- false: Disabled.

Default value: false.', example='false'),
    hostnameType?: string(name='HostnameType', description='The hostname type. Valid values:

- Custom: custom hostname.
- IpBased: IP-based hostname.
- InstanceIdBased: instance ID-based hostname.

Default value: Custom.', example='Custom'),
  }(name='PrivateDnsNameOptions', description='The private domain name configuration information of the instance.


For more information about private private domain resolution, see [Private private domain resolution for ECS](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2844797.html).', position='Query'),
  privateIpAddress?: string(name='PrivateIpAddress', description='The private IP address of the instance. When you specify system reserved IP address for a VPC-type ECS instance, the IP address must be selected from the idle CIDR block of the vSwitch (VSwitchId).

Take note of the following items:

- After PrivateIpAddress is specified:
    - If the Amount parameter is set to 1, system reserved IP address is assigned to the single ECS instance created.
    - If the Amount parameter is greater than 1, consecutive private IP addresses starting from the specified private IP address are assigned to the multiple ECS instances created in batches. Note that in this case, you cannot bind secondary ENIs to the instances (that is, you cannot specify parameters such as NetworkInterface.N.*).

-  If NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType is set to Primary, you cannot specify PrivateIpAddress. You can only specify NetworkInterface.N.PrimaryIpAddress.

>The first and the last three IP addresses of each vSwitch are reserved by the system and cannot be specified.
For example, if the CIDR block of the vSwitch is 192.168.1.0/24, the four IP addresses 192.168.1.0, 192.168.1.253, 192.168.1.254, and 192.168.1.255 are reserved by the system.', example='``10.1.**.**``', position='Query'),
  ramRoleName?: string(name='RamRoleName', description='The name of the instance RAM role. You can use the RAM API operation [ListRoles](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/28713.html) to query the instance RAM roles that you have created.', example='RAM_Name', position='Query'),
  regionId: string(name='RegionId', description='The region ID of the instance. You can call [DescribeRegions](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25609.html) to query the most recent region list.

This parameter is required.', example='cn-hangzhou', position='Query'),
  resourceGroupId?: string(name='ResourceGroupId', description='The ID of the enterprise resource group to which the instance belongs.', example='rg-bp67acfmxazb4p****', position='Query'),
  resourceOwnerAccount?: string(name='ResourceOwnerAccount', position='Query'),
  resourceOwnerId?: long(name='ResourceOwnerId', position='Query'),
  securityEnhancementStrategy?: string(name='SecurityEnhancementStrategy', description='Specifies whether to enable security hardening. Valid values:

- Active: Enables security hardening. This value takes effect only for public images.
- Deactive: Disables security hardening. This value takes effect for all image types.', example='Active', position='Query'),
  securityGroupId?: string(name='SecurityGroupId', description='The ID of the security group to which the new instance belongs. Instances in the same security group can communicate with each other. The maximum number of instances that a security group can contain depends on the security group type. For more information, see the "Security group limits" section in [Limits](~~25412#SecurityGroupQuota~~).

> SecurityGroupId determines the network type of the instance. For example, if the network type of the specified security group is VPC, the instance is a VPC-type instance, and you must also specify the VSwitchId parameter.

If you do not specify LaunchTemplateId or LaunchTemplateName to determine a launch template, the security group ID is required. Take note of the following items:

- You can specify one security group by using SecurityGroupId, or specify one or more security groups by using SecurityGroupIds.N. However, you cannot specify both SecurityGroupId and SecurityGroupIds.N at the same time.

- If NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType is set to Primary, you cannot specify SecurityGroupId or SecurityGroupIds.N. You can only specify NetworkInterface.N.SecurityGroupId or NetworkInterface.N.SecurityGroupIds.N.', example='sg-bp15ed6xe1yxeycg7****', position='Query'),
  securityGroupIds?: [ string ](name='SecurityGroupIds', description='Adds the instance to multiple security groups at the same time. The valid values of N depend on the quota of security groups that the instance can join. For more information, see [Security group limits](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/101348.html).

Note:

- You cannot specify both SecurityGroupId and SecurityGroupIds.N at the same time.
- If NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType is set to Primary, you cannot specify SecurityGroupId or SecurityGroupIds.N. You can only specify NetworkInterface.N.SecurityGroupId or NetworkInterface.N.SecurityGroupIds.N.', example='sg-bp15ed6xe1yxeycg7****', position='Query'),
  spotDuration?: int32(name='SpotDuration', description='The protection period of the spot instance. Unit: hours. Valid values:
- 1: Alibaba Cloud guarantees that the instance runs for 1 hour after creation and is not automatically released. After 1 hour, the system compares the bid price with the marketplace price and checks the resource inventory in real time to determine whether to retain or release the instance.
- 0: Alibaba Cloud does not guarantee the runtime of the instance after creation. The system compares the bid price with the marketplace price and checks the resource inventory in real time to determine whether to retain or release the instance.

Default value: 1.
> 
> - This parameter can only be set to 0 or 1.
> - Spot instances are billed by the second. We recommend that you select an appropriate protection period based on the execution duration of your specific task.
> - Alibaba Cloud sends you a notification through an ECS system event 5 minutes before the instance is released.', example='1', minimum=0, maximum=720, position='Query'),
  spotInterruptionBehavior?: string(name='SpotInterruptionBehavior', description='The break mode of the spot instance. Valid values:

- Terminate: Releases the instance.
- Stop: Puts the instance into economical mode.

  For more information about economical mode, see [Economical mode for pay-as-you-go instances](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/63353.html).

Default value: Terminate.', example='Terminate', position='Query'),
  spotPriceLimit?: float(name='SpotPriceLimit', description='The maximum hourly price of the instance. The value can have up to three decimal places. This parameter takes effect only when the SpotStrategy parameter is set to SpotWithPriceLimit.', example='0.97', minimum=0, maximum=999999, position='Query'),
  spotStrategy?: string(name='SpotStrategy', description='The bidding policy for the pay-as-you-go instance. This parameter takes effect only when the InstanceChargeType parameter is set to PostPaid. Valid values:

- NoSpot: regular pay-as-you-go instance.
- SpotWithPriceLimit: spot instance with a maximum price limit.
- SpotAsPriceGo: spot instance for which the system automatically places bids based on the current market price.

Default value: NoSpot.', example='NoSpot', position='Query'),
  storageSetId?: string(name='StorageSetId', description='The ID of the storage set.', example='ss-bp67acfmxazb4p****', position='Query'),
  storageSetPartitionNumber?: int32(name='StorageSetPartitionNumber', description='The maximum number of partitions in the storage set. Valid values: integers greater than or equal to 1.', example='2', minimum=1, position='Query'),
  tag?: [ 
    {
      key?: string(name='Key', description='The tag key of the instance, cloud disks, and primary ENI. Valid values of N: 1 to 20. The tag key cannot be an empty string. It can be up to 128 characters in length and cannot start with aliyun or acs:. It cannot contain http:// or https://.', example='TestKey'),
      value?: string(name='Value', description='The tag value of the instance, cloud disks, and primary ENI. Valid values of N: 1 to 20. The tag value can be an empty string. It can be up to 128 characters in length and cannot contain http:// or https://.', example='TestValue'),
    }
  ](name='Tag', description='The tag information of the instance, cloud disks, and primary ENI.', position='Query'),
  tenancy?: string(name='Tenancy', description='Specifies whether to create the instance on a dedicated host. Valid values:

- default: Creates the instance on a non-dedicated host.

- host: Creates the instance on a dedicated host. If you do not specify DedicatedHostId, Alibaba Cloud automatically selects a dedicated host for the instance.

Default value: default.', example='default', position='Query'),
  uniqueSuffix?: boolean(name='UniqueSuffix', description='Specifies whether to automatically append sequential suffixes to HostName and InstanceName when you create multiple instances. The sequential suffix starts from 001 and increments up to 999. Valid values:
- true: Appends sequential suffixes.
- false: Does not append sequential suffixes.

Default value: false.

If HostName or InstanceName is set in a specified sorting format without the name_suffix naming suffix, meaning the naming format is name_prefix[begin_number,bits], UniqueSuffix does not take effect, and the names are sorted only in the specified order.

For more information, see [Specify sequential instance names or hostnames](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/196048.html).', example='true', position='Query'),
  userData?: string(name='UserData', description='Instance user data of the instance. The data must be Base64-encoded. The size of instance user data cannot exceed 32 KB before Base64 encoding.

For more information about the limits, format, and execution frequency of user data, see [User data](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/49121.html).

>To ensure the security of UserData during transmission, avoid sending sensitive data such as passwords and private keys in plaintext. If you need to transmit such information, we recommend that you encrypt the data first, encode it in Base64, and then decrypt it inside the instance to ensure information security.', example='ZWNobyBoZWxsbyBlY3Mh', position='Query'),
  vSwitchId?: string(name='VSwitchId', description='The vSwitch ID. If you create a VPC-type ECS instance, you must specify a vSwitch ID. The security group and the vSwitch must belong to the same VPC. You can call the [DescribeVSwitches](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/35748.html) operation to query information about existing vSwitches.

Take note of the following items:

- If you specify the VSwitchId parameter, the ZoneId parameter must be set to the zone where the vSwitch resides. You can also leave ZoneId unspecified, and the system automatically selects the zone where the specified vSwitch resides.

- If NetworkInterface.N.InstanceType is set to Primary, you cannot specify VSwitchId. You can only specify NetworkInterface.N.VSwitchId.', example='vsw-bp1s5fnvk4gn2tws0****', position='Query'),
  zoneId?: string(name='ZoneId', description='The zone ID of the instance. You can call the [DescribeZones](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25610.html) operation to query the zone list.

> If you specify the VSwitchId parameter, the ZoneId parameter must be set to the zone where the vSwitch resides. You can also leave the ZoneId parameter unspecified, and the system automatically selects the zone where the specified vSwitch resides.

Default value: The system automatically selects a zone.', example='cn-hangzhou-g', position='Query'),
}

